This product includes work by others:

* Orion, a Bitcoin transaction viewer by Kyle Honeycutt ("coinables"), 2023 to 2024, released into the public domain under the
  Unlicense (https://unlicense.org). Hopline began as a fork of it. What remains of it here: the starting list of exchange and
  service wallets (public/data/known-addresses.js) and the early history of the repository.
* qrcode.js ("QRCode for JavaScript") by davidshimjs, MIT License, https://github.com/davidshimjs/qrcodejs
  (public/lib/qrcode.js).
* The Ransomwhere dataset (version 1.1.0, 27 October 2024) by Jack Cable and contributors, CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13999026. Hopline ships it as an optional label
  pack (public/packs/ransomwhere.js). Changes made: the addresses and ransomware families are converted to Hopline's label pack
  format, each address's recorded payments are summarised in a note, and the addresses are sorted. Nothing else is changed.
* The mining pools list at github.com/mempool/mining-pools (used by mempool.space), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2019 btc.com and
  contributors. Hopline ships the pools' reward addresses as an optional label pack (public/packs/mining-pools.js, which starts with
  the licence text). Changes made: the pool names and addresses are converted to Hopline's label pack format, and testnet addresses
  are left out.
* The UK Sanctions List, published by the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office
  (https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-uk-sanctions-list). Contains public sector information licensed under the Open
  Government Licence v3.0 (https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/). Hopline ships the Bitcoin
  addresses written in the text of its entries as a label pack (public/packs/uk-sanctions.js). Changes made: the addresses are found in
  the free text of the entries and checked, and each is labelled with the name of its entry; nothing else of the list is kept.
* A chosen part of the GraphSense TagPacks (https://github.com/graphsense/graphsense-tagpacks), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022
  Iknaio Cryptoasset Analytics GmbH and Copyright (c) 2018-2022 AIT Austrian Institute of Technology. Hopline ships ten of its packs
  (government documents and exchanges' and services' own published addresses) as an optional label pack (public/packs/graphsense.js,
  which starts with the licence text). Changes made: the tags are converted to Hopline's label pack format, and only the Bitcoin tags
  whose source link is a page of the kind each pack was chosen for are kept; each keeps its link to its source.
* The U.S. Treasury OFAC SDN list (public domain, a U.S. government work), shipped as a label pack (public/packs/ofac-sdn.js).
